{#
  A link to a file that cannot strand the installed application.

  **The defect, and why it only shows in the PWA.** The manifest declares
  « display: standalone » with « scope: / »: the window has no address
  bar and no back button, and every URL of this site stays inside it. A
  click on a file is a NAVIGATION — the window leaves the application and
  lands on the file. On iOS there is then nothing left to press: « aucun
  moyen de revenir sauf tuer l'application », reported in exactly those
  words.

  Two attributes are enough, and that is why this partial exists rather
  than a guideline:

    download                  the browser SAVES instead of navigating.
                              The window does not move. On iOS since 13.
    target/rel                the net for browsers that ignore
                              « download »: the file opens elsewhere and
                              the application stays intact behind it.

  Of ten hand-written links to /files/…, four carried « target=_blank »
  and six carried nothing. Nobody was wrong: there was no convention to
  follow. There is one now, and tests/Core/View/UxConventionsTest.php
  refuses to let another one get away.

  Parameters:
    href        the file's URL
    label       the link text; empty for a link reduced to its icon,
                in which case `aria_label` is required — an icon has no
                name (design.md §7.4)
    classes     CSS classes (default: none)
    icon        Bootstrap icon name, without the « bi- » prefix (optional)
    filename    suggested save name (optional)
    title       title attribute (optional)
    aria_label  accessible name, when the visible text is not enough —
                either there is none, or a list repeats « Télécharger »
                on every row without saying of what (optional)
#}
<a href="{{ href }}"
   class="{{ classes|default('') }}"
   {% if title is defined and title %}title="{{ title }}"{% endif %}
   {% if aria_label is defined and aria_label %}aria-label="{{ aria_label }}"{% endif %}
   download{% if filename is defined and filename %}="{{ filename }}"{% endif %}
   target="_blank" rel="noopener">
    {%- if icon is defined and icon %}<i class="bi bi-{{ icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>{% if label %} {% endif %}{% endif -%}
    {{ label }}
</a>
